WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- [Voiceover] Blast off.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.765
- [Voiceover] Astronauts have to deal

00:00:01.765 --> 00:00:03.401
with a lot of dangers in space,

00:00:03.401 --> 00:00:05.860
deadly debris, harmful cosmic rays,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.290
and sometimes a corned beef sandwich.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.506
(boom)

00:00:10.506 --> 00:00:14.089
- [Voiceover] Houston,
we've had a problem.

00:00:15.016 --> 00:00:16.076
- [Voiceover] In the 1960s at the height

00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:18.573
of the space race, space
food was either compressed

00:00:18.573 --> 00:00:23.342
into utilitarian packages
or pureed into a tube.

00:00:23.342 --> 00:00:25.293
NASA did this in part
to reduce the dangers

00:00:25.293 --> 00:00:27.375
free-floating crumbs could pose,

00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:30.276
like wreaking havoc on the
space capsule's instruments.

00:00:30.276 --> 00:00:32.961
During the Gemini 3 mission,
astronaut John Young

00:00:32.961 --> 00:00:35.374
didn't quite get the memo when he snuck

00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:38.277
a contraband corned beef
sandwich into space.

00:00:38.277 --> 00:00:40.678
Sure, the sandwich could've caused

00:00:40.678 --> 00:00:42.365
a life-threatening accident,

00:00:42.365 --> 00:00:44.540
(suspenseful music)

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.754
but hey, wouldn't you wanna know

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.894
how a sandwich tasted in space?

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:50.497
Here's how the event
played out between Young

00:00:50.497 --> 00:00:52.997
and his co-pilot Gus Grissom.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.655
- [Voiceover] Elapsed time of 02 28 25,

00:00:57.655 --> 00:00:58.905
roll left, 5-5.

00:01:00.639 --> 00:01:01.517
What is it?

00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:02.442
- [Voiceover] Corned beef sandwich.

00:01:02.442 --> 00:01:04.165
- [Voiceover] Where did it come from?

00:01:04.165 --> 00:01:05.427
- [Voiceover] I brought it with me.

00:01:05.427 --> 00:01:07.038
Let's see how it tastes.

00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:08.050
(biting)

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.309
It smells, doesn't it?

00:01:09.309 --> 00:01:10.142
(groan)

00:01:10.142 --> 00:01:10.975
- [Voiceover] Yep.

00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:11.808
It's breaking up.

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:12.708
- [Voiceover] Is it?

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:14.885
- [Voiceover] I'm gonna
stick it in my pocket.

00:01:14.885 --> 00:01:16.601
- [Voiceover] It was a thought anyway.

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:17.671
- [Voiceover] Yep.

00:01:17.671 --> 00:01:19.276
- [Voiceover] Not a very good one.

00:01:19.276 --> 00:01:20.698
- [Voiceover] And NASA and Congress didn't

00:01:20.698 --> 00:01:21.971
think so either.

00:01:21.971 --> 00:01:23.530
Young was reprimanded for his actions

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.000
but luckily for him, the incident
didn't derail his career.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.198
He later was part of the Apollo 16 mission

00:01:29.198 --> 00:01:32.238
and walked on the moon,
but that time he made sure

00:01:32.238 --> 00:01:34.205
to leave his packed lunch at home.

00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:38.372
- [Voiceover] Tranquility Base
here, the Eagle has landed.

